---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';

export const lastUpdated = '2026-10-15';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service — Using DevSnap"
  description="The terms that apply when you use the DevSnap developer tools. Plain language, no traps, and no warranty of any kind."
  schemas={{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Terms of Service — Using DevSnap',
    url: `${SITE.domain}/terms/`,
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: SITE.author },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.publisher },
  }}
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
    <ol class="crumbs">
      <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
      <li>Terms of Service</li>
    </ol>

    <header class="tool-hero">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Plain language, no traps. If you use the site, you accept these terms. If you
        do not agree, please stop using it.
      </p>
      <p class="updated-note">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose mt-3">
      <h2>1. The service</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} provides free browser-based developer tools and written guides. The
        tools run on your device. We host the pages and the advertising that funds
        them.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        The tools are provided for lawful technical work. You agree not to use them to
        break the law, to infringe somebody else's rights, to attack third-party
        systems, or to generate fraudulent documents, forged credentials or deceptive
        material intended to cause harm.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reverse engineering a tool's output for interoperability is fine. Using a tool
        to produce material intended to deceive a person or a system is not.
      </p>

      <h2>3. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The tools are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
        implied, including the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
        particular purpose and non-infringement.
      </p>
      <p>
        They are utilities, and utilities can be wrong. A formatter can mangle a
        corner case, a regex engine can differ from the one in your runtime, and a date
        calculation can miss an edge. Verify anything that matters before you rely on
        it. This is a general statement of how software works, not an excuse for a
        known defect — if you find one, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect,
        incidental, special, consequential or exemplary damages, or for any loss of
        profits, revenue, data or goodwill, arising from your use of the site or of any
        tool on it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Availability</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided on an "as available" basis. We do not guarantee that it
        will be uninterrupted, that every tool will always work, or that we will
        keep any particular tool at all.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The site displays third-party advertising. We do not endorse the products or
        services that appear in those advertisements, and we are not responsible for
        the content of third-party sites you follow from an advertisement.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The site, its name, its design and the text of its guides belong to
        {SITE.publisher}. The tools themselves are provided for use, and you are free
        to use their output for anything, including commercially.
      </p>
      <p>
        Product names, logos and trademarks mentioned in the documentation belong to
        their respective owners and are used for identification only.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        We link to other websites where it helps. We do not control them and are not
        responsible for their content, their privacy practices or their availability.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. The date at the top of this page always reflects
        the current version, and continued use after a change means you accept it.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
